  as configured by sherpa-onnx for these models.

Silero-VAD — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  Voice-activity detection — the `vad` audio-editing commands and the `asr`
  preprocessing stage (`--vad`) — ports the Silero-VAD v5 model and its
  `get_speech_timestamps` algorithm. The model weights
  (trakktor_core/src/vad/assets/silero_vad_16k.safetensors, ~1.24 MB) are
  embedded in the binary.

Silero Stress — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-stress
  The `text stress` operation — and, through it, the automatic stress marking of
  the `tts espeech` engine — ports the Russian accentor of Silero Stress: the
  character-n-gram embedding bag with its stress and `yo` heads, the
  `rubert-tiny`-class homograph solver with its `[HOMO]`-marker head, the
  word-level marking rules, and the lookup tables that go with them. The model
  (`accentor.pt`, tag v1.4) is downloaded from GitHub at runtime, converted in
  place into the layout the runtimes read, and is not redistributed in this
  repository.

whisper.cpp / ggml — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
  https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
  The approach for feeding detected speech into transcription (a dense
  speech-only buffer with timestamp remapping) follows whisper.cpp.

