1-800-BAD-CODE punctuation / true-casing model — Apache-2.0 License
  Copyright (c) 1-800-BAD-CODE
  https://huggingface.co/1-800-BAD-CODE/xlm-roberta_punctuation_fullstop_truecase
  The `text punctuate` model — a multilingual XLM-RoBERTa encoder with a cascade
  of punctuation, true-casing, and sentence-boundary heads (the NeMo
  `PunctCapSegModel` / `ConditionedPCSDecoder`) — is ported from this
  checkpoint. Its post-processing (windowing, overlap stitching, and text
  reconstruction) follows the author's `punctuators` package (MIT License,
  https://github.com/1-800-BAD-CODE/punctuators). The PyTorch model weights
  (inside the NeMo archive) and the SentencePiece model are downloaded from
  Hugging Face at runtime and are not redistributed in this repository.

Qwen3-TTS — Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (c) 2026 Alibaba Cloud / the Qwen team
  https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS
  The `tts qwen3-tts` engine ports the Qwen3-TTS 12 Hz synthesis pipeline from
  the reference `qwen-tts` package: the dual-track talker, the residual code
  predictor, and the causal-convolutional codec decoder. The model checkpoints
  (`Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-*-CustomVoice`), each bundling the matching speech
  tokenizer (`Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz`) and the byte-level BPE vocabulary, are
  downloaded from Hugging Face at runtime and are not redistributed in this
  repository. Technical report: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.15621

F5-TTS — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2024 Yushen Chen
  https://github.com/SWivid/F5-TTS
  The `tts espeech` engine ports the F5-TTS synthesis pipeline: the
  diffusion-transformer (DiT) backbone with its ConvNeXt-V2 text encoder, the
  flow-matching sampler (Euler solver, sway-sampled timesteps, classifier-free
  guidance), and the inference-side duration estimate and chunk budget.
  Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06885

ESpeech-TTS-1 — Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (c) 2025 ESpeech
  https://huggingface.co/ESpeech
  The Russian checkpoints the `tts espeech` engine runs (`ESpeech-TTS-1_RL-V2`,
  `_RL-V1`, `_SFT-256K`, `_SFT-95K`, `_podcaster`, each with its character
  vocabulary) are trained on the F5-TTS architecture. They are downloaded from
  Hugging Face at runtime, converted in place to the moving-average weights
  inference uses, and are not redistributed in this repository.

Vocos — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2023 Charactr Inc. / gemelo.ai
  https://github.com/gemelo-ai/vocos
  The `tts espeech` engine ports the Vocos vocoder — its ConvNeXt backbone and
  the head that predicts a complex spectrum — and takes the mel filterbank and
  analysis window from its checkpoint. The weights
  (`charactr/vocos-mel-24khz`, MIT) are downloaded from Hugging Face at runtime
  and are not redistributed in this repository.
  Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.00814

candle / candle-transformers — Apache-2.0 OR MIT License
  Copyright (c) The candle authors (Hugging Face)
  https://github.com/huggingface/candle
  The vendored neural-network implementations — the Whisper and XLM-RoBERTa
  forward passes — are adapted from candle-transformers (the burn variants of
  the Whisper and XLM-RoBERTa networks are ported from that adaptation). The
  XLM-RoBERTa encoder is shared by `text structify` and `text punctuate` (the
  latter adds the cascaded classification heads). candle is also the runtime
  that executes them.

burn — Apache-2.0 OR MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2022 Nathaniel Simard & Burn Framework Contributors
  https://github.com/tracel-ai/burn
  The alternative `asr whisper`, `asr gigaam`, `asr vosk`, `text structify`,
  `text punctuate`, `tts qwen3-tts`, and `tts espeech` runtimes
  (`--runtime burn`) execute the Whisper, GigaAM, Zipformer2, SaT, punctuation,
  Qwen3-TTS, and F5-TTS/Vocos networks on burn's ndarray (CPU) and wgpu/Metal
  backends.

XLM-RoBERTa (FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base) — MIT License
  https://huggingface.co/FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base
  Used as the tokenizer for `text structify` (its tokenizer.json is downloaded
  at runtime) and as the base model of both the SaT checkpoints and the
  1-800-BAD-CODE punctuation checkpoint (whose SentencePiece model is a
  repackaging of the XLM-RoBERTa one).


